      {
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "More than just pretty photos  ",
        "body": "Despite the inherent disruption of a photographer moving through a working shop floor, every business owner at Dickson welcomed me with remarkable warmth — a generosity that occasionally extended to treats and genuine smiles I wasn't expecting. There's something quietly profound about being invited, however briefly, into the rhythm of someone's livelihood. It also raises a question I find myself returning to: how much visual documentation do businesses like these actually have of themselves? Some operators understand instinctively that strong imagery is an asset — that it shapes how the world perceives them before a single word is spoken. For others, it remains an afterthought, easily deferred. My hope is that work like this shifts that equation — that when people see what's possible, and receive something they're genuinely proud of, the value of that investment becomes self-evident."
      },
